the target language is: prolog.

% lib/feel used as a translated DMN model uses it: FEEL's built-in functions
% as templates, several of them functions written as operands.

the knowledge base uses_feel includes these resources:
    feel.

the templates are:
    the item checked is *a value*.
    the dates agree.
    every answer is yes.

the knowledge base uses_feel includes:

the item checked is a value if
    the item at position 2 of the list [10, 20, 30] is the value.

the dates agree if
    the date written as "2024-02-29" is a date
    and the date of year 2024 month 2 day 29 is the date.

every answer is yes if
    the conjunction of the list [true, true] is true
    and the disjunction of the list [false, true] is true
    and the median of the list [3, 1, 2, 4] is 2.5
    and the rounding of 1.125 away from zero to 2 decimals is 1.13
    and the rounding of 1.125 to 2 decimals half toward zero is 1.12
    and the part of "foobar" before "bar" is "foo"
    and the sublist of [1, 2, 3, 4] from position -2 with length 1 is [3]
    and "foobar" starts with "foo"
    and 3 is odd.

scenario lib is:
    item expects answers ["the item checked is 20"].
    dates expects answers ["the dates agree"].
    yes expects answers ["every answer is yes"].

query item is: the item checked is which value.
query dates is: the dates agree.
query yes is: every answer is yes.
